<h1 class="chapter-break">CHAPTER 3: SYSTEM ANALYSIS AND DESIGN</h1>
<h3>3.1 Requirement Analysis</h3>
<h4>3.1.1 Functional Requirements</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>FR-1 (Multi-Modal Ingestion):</strong> The system shall accept news input via raw text copy-paste, direct public URLs, batch CSV files, and browser extension payloads.</li>
<li><strong>FR-2 (SSRF Protection):</strong> The URL extraction module shall validate all destination IP addresses, blocking private, loopback, link-local, and cloud-provider metadata endpoints.</li>
<li><strong>FR-3 (Dual-Track ML Inference):</strong> The system shall provide stylistic NLP predictions using both a fine-tuned DistilBERT sequence classifier and calibrated classical TF-IDF models, supporting automatic fallback.</li>
<li><strong>FR-4 (Token Attribution Heatmap):</strong> The system shall compute and return word-level mathematical attribution coefficients indicating whether specific tokens pushed the prediction toward &quot;fake&quot; or &quot;real&quot;.</li>
<li><strong>FR-5 (Proposition Extraction):</strong> The claim engine shall segment articles into grammatical sentences and isolate verifiable empirical assertions using linguistic reporting verbs and numerical entity markers.</li>
<li><strong>FR-6 (Multi-Source Evidence Retrieval):</strong> The system shall query the Google Fact Check Tools API, live search feeds, and an offline baseline verification index to gather corroborating citations.</li>
<li><strong>FR-7 (Lexical Stance Detection):</strong> The evidence service shall classify retrieved third-party snippets into stance categories: <code>supports</code>, <code>contradicts</code>, or <code>inconclusive</code>.</li>
<li><strong>FR-8 (Domain Reputation Forensics):</strong> The system shall analyze article domain origins, classifying them into <code>ESTABLISHED_NEWS</code>, <code>OFFICIAL</code>, <code>RESEARCH_ORGANIZATION</code>, <code>SATIRE_PARODY</code>, <code>SUSPICIOUS</code>, or <code>UNKNOWN</code>.</li>
<li><strong>FR-9 (Multi-Signal Decision Synthesis):</strong> The decision engine shall synthesize text predictions, domain authority, and claim stances into calibrated verdicts (<code>LIKELY_REAL</code>, <code>LIKELY_FAKE</code>, <code>UNCERTAIN</code>).</li>
<li><strong>FR-10 (User Authentication &amp; Audit Trail):</strong> The system shall provide secure JWT-based registration, authentication, and private analysis history storage.</li>
</ul>
<h4>3.1.2 Non-Functional Requirements</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>NFR-1 (Performance &amp; Latency):</strong> Ingestion and classification of public URLs shall complete in under $3.0$ seconds under normal network conditions.</li>
<li><strong>NFR-2 (Reliability &amp; Graceful Degradation):</strong> If deep learning transformer models or external search APIs are unavailable, the system shall seamlessly fall back to classical models and offline knowledge bases without crashing.</li>
<li><strong>NFR-3 (Security &amp; Sanitization):</strong> User inputs shall be sanitized against injection attacks; CORS headers shall restrict unauthorized origins; password hashing shall employ PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with at least 100,000 iterations.</li>
<li><strong>NFR-4 (Explainability &amp; Usability):</strong> Visual attribution heatmaps and limitations disclaimers shall accompany every result to ensure transparency.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
