<h3>4.2 Security Architecture &amp; SSRF-Protected Ingestion Engine</h3>
<p>Allowing a server to fetch arbitrary user-supplied URLs introduces <strong>Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)</strong> vulnerabilities, wherein an attacker tricks the server into scanning private internal microservices (e.g., <code>127.0.0.1:8000</code>, <code>192.168.1.1</code>, or AWS metadata <code>169.254.169.254</code>).</p>
<p>Veritas enforces multi-tier security in [security.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/app/core/security.py):</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Hostname &amp; Scheme Whitelisting:</strong> Enforces <code>http</code> or <code>https</code> schemes; blocks internal DNS names (<code>localhost</code>, <code>*.internal</code>, <code>*.local</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Pre-Flight DNS Resolution &amp; IP Filtering:</strong> Resolves the hostname via <code>socket.getaddrinfo()</code> and evaluates every resolved IP address using Python's <code>ipaddress</code> module:<pre><code class="language-python">for info in infos:
    ip = ipaddress.ip_address(info[4][0])
    if (ip.is_private or ip.is_loopback or ip.is_link_local or ip.is_reserved):
        raise ValueError(&quot;URL resolves to a private or reserved network address&quot;)
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><strong>Anti-Tarpitting Header Normalization:</strong> In [url_fetch.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/app/services/url_fetch.py), the client uses clean desktop headers (<code>User-Agent</code>, <code>Accept</code>, <code>Accept-Language</code>), avoiding synthetic client hints (<code>Sec-Ch-Ua</code>) that cause commercial news firewalls to throttle requests.</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h3>4.3 Machine Learning Pipeline &amp; Training Module</h3>
<p>The machine learning pipeline in [ml/](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/ml) supports classical and deep sequence training:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Preprocessing:</strong> Strips markup noise, normalizes unicode punctuation (NFKC), and eliminates duplicate texts while preserving Indic script characters.</li>
<li><strong>Classical Pipeline:</strong> Trains a unigram/bigram TF-IDF vectorizer ($N=10,000$ features) alongside Logistic Regression with $L_2$ penalty, LinearSVC with probability calibration, and Random Forest ensembles.</li>
<li><strong>DistilBERT Fine-Tuning:</strong> Fine-tunes <code>distilbert-base-uncased</code> using AdamW optimizer with weight decay ($0.01$) and linear learning rate warmup over classification heads. Checkpoints and Hugging Face <code>model.safetensors</code> are saved in [models/distilbert/](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/models/distilbert).</li>
<li><strong>Adaptive Routing:</strong> If deep learning weights are present and GPU/CPU inference permits, Veritas serves DistilBERT; if unavailable or in low-resource environments, it automatically falls back to classical TF-IDF models in sub-millisecond time.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>4.4 Proposition and Empirical Claim Extraction Engine</h3>
<p>Located in [claims.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/app/services/claims.py), the proposition engine isolates factual claims from rhetorical framing:</p>
<ul>
<li>Splits text using multilingual regex boundary rules (<code>.</code>, <code>!</code>, <code>?</code>, <code>\n</code>, and Hindi/Odia danda <code>।</code>).</li>
<li>Identifies empirical markers: reporting verbs (<em>&quot;stated&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;confirmed&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;banned&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;ordered&quot;</em>), currency symbols (<em>&quot;$&quot;, &quot;₹&quot;, &quot;€&quot;</em>), numerical statistics, and dates.</li>
<li>Computes importance scores, selecting the top propositions for live evidence search while deduplicating repetitive sentences.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>4.5 Multi-Source Evidence Retrieval &amp; Stance Detection</h3>
<p>Implemented in [evidence.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/app/services/evidence.py):</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Google Fact Check Tools API:</strong> Submits prioritized claims to search for verified journalist <code>ClaimReview</code> records.</li>
<li><strong>Live Public Search:</strong> Queries search feeds using normalized claim strings and parses snippet results.</li>
<li><strong>Verified Offline Knowledge Base:</strong> Maintains offline multilingual benchmark records so the system operates during network disconnects.</li>
<li><strong>Lexical Stance Detection:</strong> Analyzes snippet titles and descriptions for refutation keywords (<em>&quot;debunked&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;false&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;misleading&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;hoax&quot;</em>) vs. affirmation keywords (<em>&quot;confirmed&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;verified&quot;</em>, <em>&quot;announced&quot;</em>), producing stance labels: <code>supports</code>, <code>contradicts</code>, or <code>inconclusive</code>.</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h3>4.6 Multilingual Processing &amp; Language Identification</h3>
<p>Implemented in [languages.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/ml/preprocessing/languages.py):</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Zero-Dependency Script Detection:</strong> Uses Unicode codepoint ranges to detect Indian scripts:
<ul>
<li>Odia: <code>[\u0B00-\u0B7F]</code></li>
<li>Devanagari (Hindi/Marathi): <code>[\u0900-\u097F]</code></li>
<li>Bengali: <code>[\u0980-\u09FF]</code></li>
<li>Tamil: <code>[\u0B80-\u0BFF]</code>, Telugu: <code>[\u0C00-\u0C7F]</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Lexical Latin-Script Detection:</strong> Uses stop-word intersection over distinctive vocabulary tables for English, Spanish, French, and German, preventing cross-language false positives.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>4.7 Frontend Web Application &amp; WebGL 3D Visualization</h3>
<p>The React 18 single-page application is structured into modular views:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>[HomePage.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/pages/HomePage.tsx):</strong> Console supporting direct text paste, preset benchmark articles, and instant URL verification.</li>
<li><strong>[AnalyzePage.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/pages/AnalyzePage.tsx):</strong> Advanced multi-tab workbench (URL extraction, Direct text, Batch CSV verification, Model selection).</li>
<li><strong>[ResultsPage.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/pages/ResultsPage.tsx):</strong> Complete dossier rendering veracity badges, confidence gauges, extracted propositions, evidence cards, and token attribution heatmaps.</li>
<li><strong>[NewsVerification3D.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/components/NewsVerification3D.tsx):</strong> Interactive WebGL 3D canvas built with Three.js rendering a central verification sphere surrounded by orbiting authoritative wire feeds, fact-check desks, and unverified rumor nodes.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>4.8 Google Chrome Manifest V3 Browser Extension</h3>
<p>The browser extension in [extension/](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/extension) consists of:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>manifest.json</code>: Configured with Manifest V3 standards, permissions for <code>activeTab</code>, <code>contextMenus</code>, <code>storage</code>, and <code>scripting</code>.</li>
<li><code>popup.html</code> &amp; <code>popup.js</code>: Displays a sleek popup window allowing users to click <strong>&quot;Verify Current Tab&quot;</strong> or paste claims for immediate in-popup evaluation.</li>
<li><strong>Intelligent DOM Extraction Fallback:</strong> When encountering anti-bot firewalls or Web Application Firewalls (e.g., Akamai or Cloudflare bot detection on outlets like NDTV) that return HTTP 403 Forbidden to automated server-side crawlers, the extension automatically triggers a client-side DOM extraction fallback via <code>chrome.scripting.executeScript()</code>. It parses the substantive article body directly from the active browser tab where the page is already authenticated and rendered, piping the normalized text directly to <code>/api/v1/verify</code> for uninterrupted analysis.</li>
<li><code>background.js</code>: Manages context menu integration, enabling right-click instant claim verification on highlighted text across any web portal or social media feed.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h1 class="chapter-break">CHAPTER 5: TESTING AND RESULTS</h1>
<h3>5.1 Test Methodology and Testing Matrix</h3>
<p>The verification architecture was subjected to four levels of rigorous evaluation:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Unit Testing:</strong> Validating individual functions (text cleaning, SSRF validation, password hashing, token attribution).</li>
<li><strong>Integration Testing:</strong> End-to-end API client tests against FastAPI routes using <code>TestClient</code>.</li>
<li><strong>ML Benchmarking:</strong> Independent holdout test set evaluation ($20%$ holdout) computing Accuracy, Precision, Recall, $F_1$-score, and ROC-AUC.</li>
<li><strong>Live System Usability &amp; Latency Profiling:</strong> Evaluating end-to-end response times on real-world news links.</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h3>5.2 Unit and Integration Test Results</h3>
<p>All automated test suites executed with $100%$ pass rates:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Backend Test Suite (<code>pytest backend/tests</code>):</strong> <strong><code>13 / 13 passed</code></strong> in 35.4 seconds ([test_api.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/tests/test_api.py), [test_services.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/backend/tests/test_services.py)).</li>
<li><strong>Machine Learning Test Suite (<code>pytest ml/tests</code>):</strong> <strong><code>3 / 3 passed</code></strong> in 13.5 seconds ([test_preprocessing.py](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/ml/tests/test_preprocessing.py)).</li>
<li><strong>Frontend Vitest Suite (<code>npm test</code>):</strong> <strong><code>8 / 8 passed</code></strong> across 3 test files in 8.9 seconds ([HomePage.test.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/pages/HomePage.test.tsx), [AnalyzePage.test.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/pages/AnalyzePage.test.tsx), [Components.test.tsx](file:///d:/fake-news-verification/frontend/src/test/Components.test.tsx)).</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h3>5.3 Model Performance Evaluation and Confusion Matrices</h3>
<p>Models were trained on leakage-aware stratified splits ($70%$ Train, $10%$ Validation, $20%$ Test) using balanced real and fabricated articles.</p>
<p><strong>Table 5.1: Model Performance Benchmarking on Independent Holdout Test Set</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
