<h3 class="appendix-break">APPENDIX B: USER MANUAL &amp; DEPLOYMENT GUIDE</h3>
<h4>B.1 System Prerequisites</h4>
<ul>
<li>Python 3.10 / 3.11+</li>
<li>Node.js v18+ and npm</li>
<li>Operating System: Windows 10/11, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, or macOS</li>
</ul>
<h4>B.2 Installation and Setup</h4>
<pre><code class="language-bash"># 1. Clone repository and navigate to root
cd fake-news-verification

# 2. Configure Python Virtual Environment
python -m venv .venv
# Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
# Linux/Mac: source .venv/bin/activate

# 3. Install Backend Dependencies
pip install -r backend/requirements.txt

# 4. Initialize Database and Train Models
python -m ml.preprocessing.generate_sample
python -m ml.training.train_classical

# 5. Install Frontend Dependencies
cd frontend
npm install
cd ..
</code></pre>
<h4>B.3 Starting Local Development Servers</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Terminal 1 (Backend API):</strong><pre><code class="language-powershell">$env:PYTHONPATH = &quot;backend;.&quot;
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --app-dir backend
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><strong>Terminal 2 (Frontend React App):</strong><pre><code class="language-bash">cd frontend
npm run dev
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><strong>Access Points:</strong>
<ul>
<li>Web App UI: <code>http://localhost:5173</code></li>
<li>API Docs (Swagger): <code>http://localhost:8000/docs</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4>B.4 Chrome Browser Extension Installation</h4>
<ol>
<li>Open Google Chrome and navigate to <code>chrome://extensions/</code>.</li>
<li>Enable <strong>&quot;Developer mode&quot;</strong> in the top-right corner.</li>
<li>Click <strong>&quot;Load unpacked&quot;</strong> and select the <code>fake-news-verification/extension/</code> folder.</li>
<li>Pin the Veritas extension icon to your toolbar for 1-click active tab verification.</li>
</ol>
